# Ignore-file for `Dockerfile`. The build context is this repo's own root — build with
# `docker build -t tovu:local .` from inside the Tovu checkout.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore` from beside the Dockerfile and gives it
# precedence over any `.dockerignore` at the context root. See:
# https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/

# Host-built dependencies. These carry macOS/arm64 binaries for better-sqlite3,
# argon2 and sharp; shipping them into a linux image produces the classic
# "builds fine, dies on require" failure. The build stage installs fresh.
node_modules
apps/*/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated by `npm run build` and the two vite builds.
dist
apps/*/dist
apps/*/dist-debug

# sites/ — same itemized exclusions as this repo's own .gitignore (2026-08-31: "sites/ is now
# TRACKED"), and for the identical reason: a blanket `sites` pattern here excludes the WHOLE tree
# from the build context, including the one file this now needs to ship — `content.seed.db` (see
# "Ships this site's stock content seed" below, and hydrate-content-db-from-seed.ts). Docker's
# .dockerignore cannot re-include a file under a directory a broader pattern already excluded (same
# rule as .gitignore), so this MUST itemize what stays out rather than exclude the directory and try
# to negate individual files back in.
#
# Still excluded, matching .gitignore line for line:
#   - content.db itself: the developer's real, growing database (real chat transcripts, session auth
#     log, sealed provider credentials, ...) — baking it into a published image would ship their data
#     to anyone who pulls it. `npm run seed:site` produces the thing that SHOULD ship instead: a
#     pruned, VACUUMed `content.seed.db`, deliberately not matched below.
#   - WAL/shm sidecars: transient, and a sidecar shipped against a mismatched content.db corrupts
#     reads on first open.
#   - restore points + .bak snapshots: tens of MB of point-in-time DB copies, each a full binary blob.
#   - out/: build output, regenerated.
# The Dockerfile's own build stage still removes each of these again (belt and braces), so an edit
# here cannot quietly reintroduce a live db into the image either way.
sites/*/content.db
sites/*/content.db-wal
sites/*/content.db-shm
sites/*/content.db.bak-*
sites/*/restore-point-*.db
sites/*/out/

.git
.github
coverage
development/coverage
**/*.log

# Agent-framework and working docs. Large, and nothing in the image reads them.
AI-Dev-Shop
ADS-memory
foundry

# Test artifacts.
test-results
playwright-report
development/e2e
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx

# Local env files. Secrets are passed at runtime, never baked in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# mkcert dev TLS cert + PRIVATE KEY (`.certs/`, matching `.gitignore`'s `/.certs*/`). Unlike a git
# commit, `COPY . .` in the build stage above has no ignore-file inheritance from git — this repo's
# own build context is machine-local, so any contributor who has run `mkcert` for their own
# `npm run dev` and then runs `docker build` from the same checkout would otherwise bake their
# private key straight into the image. Belt-and-braces with `.gitignore`, not a substitute for it —
# this file is Docker's own ignore list and is read independently.
.certs
.certs.disabled
